---
// The Reception package page — roadmap step 2's first real output
// ("Structured package/pricing content in Sanity", see CLAUDE.md): one
// wedding package category browsable as a structured, switchable page rather
// than as pages of the printed PDF catalogue. Reception only, deliberately —
// Banquet, High Tea and Beverage are still PDF-only, and weddings.html's
// package cards link to banquet-package.html / high-tea-package.html /
// beverage-package.html, which don't exist yet. Build those three to this
// page's pattern before the site goes live.
//
// A real page at the site root as of 2026-09-23, promoted out of sandboxes/
// on request and linked live from weddings.html's Reception card. (It had
// been promoted once before, on 2026-09-22, and demoted the same day as not
// ready — this time it stays.) Deliberately NOT in the top nav: the nav is
// flat (Weddings/Corporate/Celebrations/Gallery) and CLAUDE.md's standing
// call is not to restructure it until a public packages page is actually
// greenlit. Entry point is the Reception card on weddings.html.
//
// This was originally the tier-compare half of the reception-menus.html
// sandbox, split into its own file (2026-09-18) so the tier/package work and
// the Stations work could be iterated on separately without the two fighting
// over the same file. Stations spent that time in its own sandbox — first
// sandboxes/reception-stations.html, then a rebuilt sandboxes/reception-
// stations-v2.html — and was merged back into THIS page as its closing
// section on 2026-09-30, per the standing plan CLAUDE.md had carried since
// 2026-09-23 (it's confirmed Reception-only and additive, not a fourth tier).
// What came across: the whole Stations `<section>` (stage+thumbnails on
// mobile/tablet, carousel+index on desktop, all 16 real stations), ~3200
// lines of its page-scoped CSS, and four JS controllers (stage, mobtab
// sliding-pill, carousel, and its own newer lightbox controller — see below).
// sandboxes/reception-stations-v2.html itself was deleted the same day, on
// request, once the merge had been checked live in a browser — its
// sandboxes/index.html listing was removed with it.
//
// Content is copied verbatim from docs/bacchus-wedding-catalogue.pdf (tier
// names, every menu item, the vegetarian marker — rendered here as a
// circled "V" badge rather than the catalogue's literal "(V)", see
// .package-veg-marker below) and the separately shared client
// quote (the three real per-person prices) — see CLAUDE.md "Real wedding
// package structure" and "Real per-person tier pricing". Reception, Banquet
// and High Tea are treated here as three mutually exclusive meal-format
// options (a wedding picks one), not layered courses — see CLAUDE.md for
// that assumption's basis and its "working assumption" caveat.
//
// The tier switcher reuses the homepage's existing .tab-bar/.tab-panel
// component as-is (same pill-slide JS in main.js, same mobile equal-width
// fix, same divided-list .tab-panel li styling) rather than building a new
// one — .tab-panel.full is the existing single-column modifier, used here
// instead of the homepage's two-column image+text layout. Menu-specific
// layout (price display, grouped ingredient lists) is new, page-scoped CSS
// under .package-menu-* below, following the same "own namespace" convention
// secure-booking.html already uses for page-specific sections.
//
// Section order is dark/plain/dark (tier compare → carousel → Stations) —
// closing on the on-dark Stations section right before the footer, same
// rhythm as every other real page's own close. This fixes what used to be a
// byproduct of the tier/Stations split: before the 2026-09-30 merge, this
// page closed on the plain carousel section instead, which read as an
// unfinished ending compared to every other page's dark "Visit Bacchus"
// close — flagged in this file's own history rather than fixed at the time,
// since the on-dark section that belonged there was still living in the
// sibling sandbox. It isn't any more.
//
// Each tier panel leads with three "signature dish" photo tiles (real dish
// names from that tier's own menu, chosen as its most distinctive items)
// before the full ingredient lists — reuses gallery.html's
// .gallery-item/.gallery-tag component for the hover-zoom + tag-reveal
// treatment, same visual language as the real gallery. Real photography is
// now in for all 9 (images/weddings/reception-<tier>-<dish>.webp).
//
// All 9 dish tiles, plus all 32 station figures below, open a shared
// lightbox on click. Reuses gallery.html's #lightbox markup/CSS as-is, but
// NOT its main.js controller — that one is hard-wired to a single #ggrid,
// and prev/next needs to stay within whichever group a visitor actually
// opened rather than wandering across unrelated photos. So this page has its
// own controller (bottom of the file), keyed off a repeatable data-lb-group
// instead of one fixed grid id — dishes use "daisy"/"lavender"/"rose" (3
// each), stations use "stations-hybrid-mobtab"/"stations-hybrid-desktop" (16
// each, kept as two groups rather than one combined "stations" group since
// only one half is ever visible at a time). Guarded per CLAUDE.md bug #4
// (no-ops if #lightbox or no [data-lb-group] elements exist).
//
// This controller is the Stations sandbox's own newer copy, merged in
// 2026-09-30 to replace this page's older one — it preloads/decodes each
// photo off-DOM before ever showing it (fixes a previous-photo-flashes-
// briefly bug), gives .lightbox a scroll fallback for long captions (see
// styles.css), and splits the caption's third line into two paragraphs
// (.lightbox-detail italic for a serving note, .lightbox-detail-items for a
// dotted item list with real .package-veg-marker badges). Dish tiles carry
// neither a price-shaped data-tag nor any data-detail at all, so
// applyImage() has to handle two different data shapes on one controller —
// see its own comments for exactly how (the short version: a leading €
// is what tells a station's data-tag apart from a dish's plain category
// word, and both caption paragraphs get hidden outright when empty rather
// than rendering as blank spaced lines under a dish photo).
//
// Carries the same chrome as every other real page: the shared nav (Weddings
// marked .active, since this sits under the wedding journey), the standard
// footer, and the footer's "🏖️ Sandboxes" link pointing at sandboxes/ like
// its siblings do.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import PageHero from "../../../components/PageHero.astro"
import EnquirySection from "../../../components/EnquirySection.astro"
import WaitlistPopover from "../../../components/WaitlistPopover.astro"
import ArrowIcon from "../../../components/ArrowIcon.astro"
import Lightbox from "../../../components/Lightbox.astro"
// After BaseLayout, so it loads after global.css, as the inline block did.
import "../../../styles/package-page.css"
import "../../../styles/package-stations.css"
import Photo from "../../../components/Photo.astro"
import PhotoCarousel from "../../../components/PhotoCarousel.astro"
import GalleryTile from "../../../components/GalleryTile.astro"

// The "closer look" photo strip.
const carouselSlides = [
  {
    src: "food-and-drink/canapes-service",
    alt: "A waiter serving canapés at a wedding reception",
    caption: "Canapés, Passed",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/terrace-celebration-reception",
    alt: "Guests mingling at a Bacchus wedding reception on the Terrace",
    caption: "Reception, On the Terrace",
  },
  {
    src: "food-and-drink/champagne",
    alt: "A guest raising a glass of sparkling wine at a dressed table",
    caption: "A Toast, On Arrival",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/terrace-marquee-tables",
    alt: "Tables dressed under a marquee on the Terrace",
    caption: "The Terrace, Dressed",
  },
  {
    src: "venue/secret-garden-night",
    alt: "A long candlelit table in the Secret Garden at night",
    caption: "The Secret Garden, By Night",
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Reception Menus — Package (concept) — Bacchus"
  menuBackgroundImage="weddings/cake-chandelier"
>
  <PageHero
    crumb="Reception Menus"
    parent={{ href: "/weddings", label: "Weddings" }}
    image={{
      src: "food-and-drink/canapes-tray",
      alt: "A tray of salmon canapés being served",
    }}
  >
    Our Reception <em>Menus</em>
    <Fragment slot="sub">
      Canapés passed by hand, a flying buffet, desserts and the wedding cake — taken
      standing, rather than at a seated breakfast.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="sub-secondary">
      Three considered tiers, each explored in full below — plus Stations to add on top.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="ctas">
      <a href="#enquire" class="button button-gradient button-shimmer">
        <span>Book a tasting</span>
        <ArrowIcon />
      </a>
      <a
        href="/docs/bacchus-wedding-catalogue.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="button button-ghost"
      >
        <span>View the catalogue</span>
      </a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section-padding on-dark on-dark-gold-wash" id="reception-tiers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>
        From the catalogue
      </div>
      <div class="package-tabs-grid">
        <h2 class="package-tabs-heading" data-reveal style="--d: 80ms">
          Compare the three <em>tiers</em>
        </h2>
        <div
          class="tab-bar package-tabs-tabbar"
          role="tablist"
          data-reveal
          style="--d: 160ms"
        >
          <span class="pill" id="pill"></span>
          <button class="active" data-tab="daisy" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
            Daisy
          </button>
          <button data-tab="lavender" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
            Lavender
          </button>
          <button data-tab="rose" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
            Rose
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="package-tabs-lead" data-reveal style="--d: 220ms">
          <p class="lead">
            Daisy, Lavender and Rose are three interpretations of the same reception, each
            more abundant than the last.
          </p>
          <p class="lead">
            Switch between them below — every dish is taken straight from the printed
            catalogue.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="package-tier-cards" data-reveal style="--d: 280ms">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="package-tier-card active"
          data-tier-card="daisy"
          aria-pressed="true"
        >
          <span class="package-tier-card-check" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none">
              <path
                d="M4 9.5l3 3 7-7.5"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2.4"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-eyebrow">Reception</span>
          <b class="package-tier-card-name">Daisy</b>
          <span class="package-tier-card-price">
            €53<span class="package-tier-card-unit">per person</span>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-desc">
            An elegant opening tier — ten cold and ten hot canapés, a three-dish flying
            buffet, four desserts, coffee and the wedding cake.
          </span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="package-tier-card"
          data-tier-card="lavender"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <span class="package-tier-card-check" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none">
              <path
                d="M4 9.5l3 3 7-7.5"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2.4"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-eyebrow">Reception</span>
          <b class="package-tier-card-name">Lavender</b>
          <span class="package-tier-card-price">
            €57<span class="package-tier-card-unit">per person</span>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-desc">
            A richer interpretation — the same generous structure, with each course made a
            touch more indulgent.
          </span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="package-tier-card"
          data-tier-card="rose"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <span class="package-tier-card-check" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none">
              <path
                d="M4 9.5l3 3 7-7.5"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2.4"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-eyebrow">Reception</span>
          <b class="package-tier-card-name">Rose</b>
          <span class="package-tier-card-price">
            €64<span class="package-tier-card-unit">per person</span>
          </span>
          <span class="package-tier-card-desc">
            Our most refined tier — foie gras, oysters and scallops meet a lavish flying
            buffet, desserts, coffee and cake.
          </span>
        </button>
