           above, which already shows the selected tier's name + eyebrow +
           checkmark. Commented out rather than deleted in case it's
           wanted back (e.g. as an anchor once a visitor has scrolled
           further down past the cards into the dish list, out of view
           of the checkmark) — see the reasoning discussion around this
           point. Note as of the 2026-09-22 swipe-carousel rework below,
           the script no longer has any #packageTierName-aware code at
           all (the old setTierName()/tierNameEl crossfade was removed
           along with the fade-based tier switch it supported) — so
           re-enabling this block would need new wiring, not just
           uncommenting it.
      <div class="package-now-viewing">Now viewing</div>
      <div class="capacity">
        Reception · <span id="packageTierName" class="package-tier-name">Daisy</span>
      </div>
      */}
      {/* No data-reveal here (was: data-reveal style="--d: 300ms") — the
           sitewide scroll-reveal observer (main.js, threshold: 0.18) needs
           18% of a data-reveal target's OWN height visible before firing.
           .panels wraps a whole tier's full content (3 dish photos + up
           to 6 ingredient-list groups), so its height varies a lot by
           tier and by viewport (much taller once .package-menu-groups
           collapses to 1 column on mobile) — 18% of that was a large,
           inconsistent scroll distance before anything appeared, reading
           as "content stays hidden too long". The heading/tab-bar/lead
           directly above already carry their own compact, well-behaved
           reveals that cue "this section is arriving"; .panels itself
           doesn't need a second scroll-gated fade on top of that. Same
           reasoning CLAUDE.md already documents for why the dish tiles
           skip data-reveal entirely (display:none tab-panels never fire
           the observer) — this component just doesn't suit the generic
           reveal mechanism. */}
